    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32009" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">obtūsĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		obtundo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a crushing</i>, 
			<i>bruising</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">membri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Res. Carn. 57</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Bluntness</i>, <i>dulness</i> (eccl.
			Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">obtusio sensuum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 3, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Cael.
					Aur. Tard. 1, 1, 6</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">visus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 1, 1, 5</span></i>
			.— <b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>, <i><span class="en">Cael. Aur. Tard. 2, 6, 91</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 4, 62</span></i>.</div>
